+## 2026-10-23T20:19:34.9088008+08:00 (UTC+08:00) - Preserve complete MySQL command history
+
+- Reproduced native command truncation on real MySQL 8.4.13: VARCHAR(256) plus INSERT IGNORE commits shortened text and leaves no pending work. Actual inputs are 23, 1,032 and 69,025 UTF-8 bytes, each within the native UTF-16 packet bound. The unchanged provider fails the same final audit bytecode retained for before/after review.
+- Version .9 creates MEDIUMTEXT and widens known legacy VARCHAR/TEXT command columns while preserving actual charset/collation. Existing MEDIUMTEXT/LONGTEXT remains intact; unsupported narrow custom attributes reject visibly. Command inserts use plain INSERT. No lost suffix is invented and SQLite command SQL is unchanged.
+- Schema initialization now owns/closes statements, fences SQL/runtime failures, attempts rollback and cannot report ready afterward. MySQL implicit DDL commits remain a documented boundary; the fence cannot undo earlier successful DDL.
+- Java 21 NeoForge build succeeds. Actual provider/SQLite storage suite passes 156 assertions across 32 databases. Actual provider/Connector-J 8.4.0/MySQL suite passes 38 lock, batch constraint, owned binary/UTF-8, actual-commit/injected-reply-loss and public read-isolation assertions. Only the standalone Minecraft bootstrap/logger owner is substituted.
+- Fresh native MySQL command/schema/restart checks pass 76 assertions, and normal logging/rollback/commerce/restart adds 45. Four command cases cover new schema, legacy VARCHAR, legacy TEXT and preserved larger LONGTEXT/custom comment; narrow custom schema rejection preserves original input. Root project records independent SQL dumps, same-container restart and additional SQLite/native regressions separately.
+- No production deployment, physical client acceptance, all-backend equivalence, sustained load/retention, forced database crash, real network loss or unavailable migration completion is claimed. Preserve the original failure and all fixture evidence. Author and committer: A-BenLi06 <ben_li06@outlook.com>.
